  "rationale": "Model sensing and motion as separate plants, then use compact specifications to enforce safe obstacle recovery, one-shot action commits, strong forward-progress bias in clear space, brief directed turns on side obstacles, rare backward escape only for front blockage, and last-resort full rotation only after repeated front-blocked failures.",
  "strategy": [
    "Use a sensor plant for uncontrollable perception outcomes and a motion plant for available controllable pulses.",
    "Use one policy specification with perception/decision and one-shot action states so each non-branching state enables exactly one controllable action.",
